{"text": "DEPOSITION SUMMARY (PAGE:LINE)                         PRIVILEGED -- PREPARED FOR TRIAL COUNSEL\n\nCase:        Kowalczyk v. Brightpath Home Care, LLC, et al.\nCourt:       Court of Common Pleas, Westmoreland County, Pa., No. 2025-CV-03381\nDeponent:    WALTER J. KOWALCZYK (Plaintiff)\nTaken:       February 24, 2026, 9:42 a.m. - 2:15 p.m., at the offices of O'Brien & Stanek, P.C.,\n             35 West Pittsburgh Street, 2nd Fl., Greensburg, PA 15601\nNoticed by:  Defendants, under Pa.R.C.P. 4007.1\nAppearances: Colleen O'Brien, Esq. (for Plaintiff); Sanjay Venkataraman, Esq., Venkataraman Lowe LLP\n             (for Brightpath Home Care, LLC); no appearance for Defendant Mullins (pro se, served)\nReporter:    Marlene Fitch, RPR\nSummarized by: jdl, 3/2/26            Our file: OS-25-0447\n\nNOTE FOR CO'B: witness tired noticeably after lunch (see 118:4 onward). He is a\ngood witness on the big points. Weak spots flagged with **.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPAGE:LINE     SUMMARY\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5:1-7:20      Background. Deponent is ninety-one years old, born August 3, 1934 in Monessen.\n              Has lived alone at 212 Sycamore St., Latrobe, since his wife Irene died\n              on 11/2/2019. Everyone calls him \"Buddy.\" One child, Barbara Kowalczyk-Greene\n              (\"Babs\"), who lives in Scottsdale with her husband Dennis Greene.\n\n8:1-10:14     Work history. 38 years as a millwright; receives a union pension through\n              Steel & Tin Workers Local 1408 of $1,412 a month plus Social Security of\n              $2,236. Both are direct-deposited to Monongahela Valley Federal Credit Union\n              (\"Mon Valley FCU\"), where he has banked \"since Eisenhower.\"\n\n10:15-13:6    Health. Has macular degeneration (cannot read small print without a\n              magnifier), wears hearing aids, takes warfarin and a \"water pill.\" PCP is\n              Dr. Hye-Jin Park at Chestnut Ridge Medical Center. Denies any memory\n              problem. ** Admits Dr. Park gave him \"the clock test\" last fall and told\n              him he had mild cognitive impairment; he disagrees with that.\n\n13:7-19:22    Hiring Brightpath. After a fall in March 2025 he spent four days at\n              Chestnut Ridge. Babs arranged home care by phone from Arizona. Contract\n              signed April 1, 2025 (Exhibit 3): three visits a week at $34.50 an hour.\n              Brightpath assigned Tiffany-Rae Mullins. He liked her; \"she was like a\n              granddaughter.\" She started driving him to Mass at St. Stanislaus on Sundays\n              in his Buick.\n\n20:1-27:9     Access to finances. By June Ms. Mullins was picking up his mail and\n              \"helping with the bills.\" He gave her his debit card to buy groceries and\n              told her the PIN, 0834 (\"my birthday, so I don't forget it\").\n              Card number per Exhibit 5: 4989 4186 6411 9402, exp. 09/27. He kept his\n              online banking password on a sticky note on the refrigerator; he recited it\n              as Polka1934! and his user name as buddyk34.\n              ** Concedes he never told her NOT to use the card for herself.\n\n27:10-41:3    The withdrawals. Shown Exhibit 7 (statements for share draft account\n              00-4471-208816). Does not recognize:\n                - 31 ATM withdrawals, May 29 through Sept. 30, 2025, totaling $15,340;\n                - check no. 3318 for $9,800.00 payable to \"T. Mullins\", memo \"loan\";\n                - check no. 3321 for $4,250 to Laurel Highlands Coin & Jewelry;\n                - an online transfer of $22,000 on 10/14/25 to an account ending 7706.\n              Signature on 3318 \"looks like mine but I never wrote that.\" Denies ever\n              lending money to Tiffany. ** On cross-check with 34:11, he first said he\n              \"might have helped her with her car once,\" then said that was fifty dollars\n              for gas.\n\n41:4-48:16    The new phone. In August Ms. Mullins bought him a smartphone \"so Babs could\n              see me on the video.\" He does not know how to use it for banking. Exhibit 9\n              (credit union device log) shows the mobile app was enrolled on 8/19/2025 from\n              a phone with IMEI 35 693803 564380 9, and that later logins came from IP\n              addresses 198.51.100.23 and 2001:db8:4c2:91::1f. He has no internet at the house.\n              His own number is 724-555-0142; the app was registered to (724) 555-0190,\n              which he does not recognize.\n\n48:17-55:2    Discovery of the loss. On October 20, 2025, teller Chase Dombrowski at the\n              Latrobe branch asked him about the $22,000 transfer when he came in for\n              cash. \"Chase turned the screen around and I about fell over.\" Balance\n              was $611.08; a year earlier it had been \"over sixty thousand.\"\n              He called Barbara from the branch.\n\n55:3-63:18    Aftermath. Babs flew in on Oct. 22. Police report made to Latrobe PD,\n              Det. Ray Santangelo, incident no. 25-LP-009214. Mon Valley FCU\n              fraud claim no. FRD-2025-11873 denied in part because the PIN was\n              \"voluntarily shared.\" Brightpath terminated Ms. Mullins 10/24/2025.\n              He understands she has been charged (18 Pa.C.S. § 3921) and that she has\n              a prior theft conviction from Fayette County that the agency missed.\n\n63:19-71:5    What Brightpath knew. He complained twice to the scheduler that Tiffany\n              came on days she wasn't scheduled and brought her boyfriend, Kyle. No one\n              called back. ** Cannot give dates. Thinks one call was \"around the\n              Fourth of July.\" Brightpath's office number, which he dialed from memory:\n              724 555 0117.\n\n71:6-80:12    Church and giving. Father Zielinski of St. Stanislaus Kostka Parish visited\n              weekly. Deponent tithes $40 a week by envelope and denies\n              authorizing the $1,500 online gift to the parish roof fund on Exhibit 7\n              (\"I'd have done it by check\"). Venkataraman pressed on whether deponent\n              gives money away freely; he also gave $200 to the county Democratic committee\n              in 2024 \"like every election year.\"\n\n80:13-96:7    Damages. Total he believes was taken: $52,890 (matches our schedule).\n              Has had trouble sleeping, lost eleven pounds, stopped going to the\n              Tuesdays card game at the union hall because he is \"ashamed.\" Dr. Park\n              started him on mirtazapine 15 mg in November. Babs now pays his\n              bills remotely; he resents it.\n\n96:8-117:20   Cross by Mr. Venkataraman. Established: (a) deponent signed the Brightpath\n              service agreement without reading the \"no financial assistance\" clause,\n              could not read it without his magnifier; (b) he gave Ms. Mullins a\n              Christmas card with $100 cash in 2024 -- before she was assigned to him,\n              when she cared for a neighbor; (c) he told Babs in July everything was\n              \"fine\"; (d) he could not name the current month without prompting\n              (objection, O'Brien; he then answered correctly).\n\n118:4-131:2   ** After lunch. Confused Exhibit 5 with Exhibit 7. Said the debit card\n              \"ends in 9402 or 4902.\" Said Irene \"handles the checkbook,\" then corrected\n              himself. Ms. O'Brien requested a break at 124:15.\n\n              Asked about insurance: he has Medicare and a supplemental plan through\n              the Local, member no. STW-1408-00771; neither covered the home care, which\n              Babs paid from her own account ($1,656 for the first month). He also said\n              Ms. Mullins once drove him to Laurel Highlands \"to look at Irene's rings\" and\n              that he has not seen Irene's engagement ring since. He does not know\n              whether it was sold. (New fact; not in our complaint. Consider amending.)\n\n131:3-140:9   Redirect. Reaffirmed he never authorized any withdrawal over \"grocery\n              money,\" never wrote check 3318, never used the app. Identified his own\n              signature exemplar (Exhibit 12). Read and sign reserved.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFOLLOW-UP\n 1. Subpoena carrier records for (724) 555-0190 -- likely Kyle Mullins.\n 2. Get Dr. Park's chart; expect defense IME request on capacity. Retain geriatric psych.\n 3. Ask Dombrowski for a statement before the credit union lawyers get to him.\n 4. Form 1099-R for the pension shows the Local 1408 plan ID; redact before producing.\n 5. Babs's contact for scheduling: babs.kg@desertmail.example, 480.555.0163.\n 6. Errata sheet due 30 days after transcript; calendar for April 6, 2026.", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "1,210 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Walter J. Kowalczyk", "Barbara Kowalczyk-Greene", "Dennis Greene", "Tiffany-Rae Mullins", "Ms. Mullins", "Tiffany", "Chase Dombrowski", "Barbara", "Babs", "Latrobe PD", "Ray Santangelo", "Kyle", "Father Zielinski", "Venkataraman", "Mr. Venkataraman", "Dr. Park", "Ms. O'Brien", "Irene", "Kyle Mullins"], "companies": ["Brightpath Home Care, LLC", "Steel & Tin Workers", "Monongahela Valley Federal Credit Union", "Chestnut Ridge Medical Center", "Laurel Highlands Coin & Jewelry", "Predix Financial", "Mon Valley FCU", "Brightpath", "St. Stanislaus Kostka Parish", "county Democratic committee", "Union hall", "Medicare", "Local", "desertmail"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Monessen", "Latrobe", "Scottsdale", "Greensburg", "Pennsylvania", "St. Stanislaus Kostka Parish", "Fayette County", "Union hall", "Laurel Highlands"], "health": ["macular degeneration